Theorem RL-12: cross-block donor-to-recipient owner-credit transfer

  Preconditions:
    - The donor block dominates the recipient block.
    - The recipient block post-dominates the donor on normal paths.
    - Donor and recipient have the same loop multiplicity.
    - The donor is statically Unique and no unwind can strand the transfer.

  Soundness property:
    Forall dying donor d and fresh same-type recipient r across blocks:
      (P1) RL-12 freezes transfer iff every path/multiplicity condition holds.
      (P2) the exact donor owner credit becomes the recipient's credit.
      (P3) the relation is evaluator-equivalent to independent birth and release.
    Physical storage reuse is a later projection.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate:
      all_constraints_hold_credit_transfer -> transfer
      no_dominance_no_transfer -> no transfer
      no_postdominance_no_transfer -> no transfer
      different_loop_no_transfer -> no transfer
      throw_on_path_no_transfer -> no transfer
      non_unique_no_transfer -> no transfer
    Coverage gate: 6 cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl12_cross_block_reuse)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-12 freezes cross-block donor/recipient owner-credit transfer in six exhaustive cases without selecting storage recycling
